# Environment variables required by the Phase 3B Supabase backend.
#
# This file lists variable NAMES only. It contains no values, and no real
# value may ever be committed here (docs/SECURITY.md §4). Copy to
# .env.local — which is git-ignored — and fill in from the Supabase
# dashboard once a project exists.
#
# STATUS: no Supabase project is provisioned or linked yet, so nothing in
# the application reads these today (see docs/PROJECT_STATE.md).

# --- Public: sent to the browser -------------------------------------
# Safe to expose. The anon/publishable key carries no privileges of its
# own — Row Level Security is what constrains it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Server-only: must never reach the browser ------------------------
# Full RLS bypass. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Imported only from
# modules guarded by the `server-only` package so that a client import
# fails the build instead of shipping the key (docs/SECURITY.md S-3).
# Expected to be needed by at most two paths: notification dispatch and
# account administration.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Conditional: booking-expiry sweep --------------------------------
# Only required if the expiry sweep (docs/DATABASE.md §7.7) is run as a
# scheduled route handler rather than via pg_cron inside Postgres. The
# mechanism has not been chosen — that decision belongs to the phase that
# can actually test it. If a route handler is used, this shared secret
# stops the endpoint being invocable by anyone who knows the URL.
# CRON_SECRET=
